RISE H100 local execution launcher for Steps 16/17.

The active scripts are:

```text
run_step16_17.sh
run_multi_model_inference.sh
compression/compression_step_16.sh
compression/compression_step_17.sh
calibrate_step17_batch_sizes.sh
compare_step17_batch_calibration.py
build_prompt_manifest_sample.py
calibrate_prompt_token_budget.py
```

Post-smoke input/output token calibration is intentionally independent from
the pipeline. Run it after Step 17 inside the same RISE vLLM environment so it
can load the exact tokenizer used by the model:

```bash
python /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/calibrate_prompt_token_budget.py
```

Before execution, edit the `USER CONFIGURATION` block at the beginning of the
script. It contains the Prompt Unit manifest path, exact model/tokenizer path,
Step 17 run directory, report output directory and the optional calibration
parameters. The utility intentionally has no CLI parameters.

The utility reads the manifest and Step 17 artifacts without changing them. It
measures input characters against Step 17's real chat-template token count,
tokenizes every raw response, reports token-limit proximity, JSON/string
truncation evidence and recorded `finish_reason` when available, and returns
one directly applicable pair: `chars_per_token_estimate` from real input
evidence and `output_token_estimation_safety_factor` from the larger of:

- the exact-tokenizer hexadecimal/output-density bound;
- the observed generated-token expansion relative to the compact output JSON
  used by the planner.

The second bound captures pretty-printed JSON, Markdown wrappers, explanations
and repeated candidates that are absent from the compact planner serialization.
The utility emits JSONL, CSV, JSON, and Markdown reports. Current Step 17
artifacts do not always persist
`finish_reason`; in that case the report marks it unavailable and keeps
probable-truncation classification separate from observed facts.

For payload-capable output-budget smoke tests, build one deterministic
two-panel sample from a complete Step 16 manifest:

```bash
python3 /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/build_prompt_manifest_sample.py \
  --input-manifest /path/to/full_step16_run/prompt_units_manifest_v2.json \
  --output-manifest /path/to/payload_budget_sample_512.json \
  --sample-size 512 \
  --representative-size 256 \
  --sample-method payload_budget_stratified \
  --max-per-parent 2 \
  --minimum-per-stratum 4 \
  --report-path /path/to/payload_budget_sample_512.sample_report.json
```

The representative panel is stratified by editable-target shape and
within-shape planned-output-token quartile. Selection is deterministic and
prioritizes Parent Group diversity. The disjoint stress panel assigns half of
its capacity to high-output payload-only units, one quarter to high-output
mixed units and one quarter to payload-capable units with the largest
authorized hexadecimal replacement. A deterministic risk-ranked fill handles
undersized pools.

The output manifest does not add fields to individual Prompt Units. Exact
panel/component membership and selection parameters are stored in the sidecar
JSON report and copied into manifest metadata. Analyze the representative and
stress panels separately. This method requires a complete Step 16 manifest; a
prefix-limited Step 16 run cannot sample the full population.

`run_multi_model_inference.sh` is the sequential multi-model orchestrator. Its
first section is intentionally edited before each experiment and controls:

- enabled models;
- `smoke` or `full` execution;
- smoke limits, including a separate Qwen limit;
- experiment/config/model paths and model-specific batch sizes;
- optional Step 16 reuse through `SKIP_STEP16` and model-specific prompt paths;
- optional prompt-only execution through `SKIP_STEP17`;
- whether the queue continues after one model fails.

The active Flow-context-aware `prompt_target_context = 4096` smoke profile uses
batch size `192` for Llama-3.1-8B, `224` for both Gemma models, and `8` for
Qwen3-32B. The safe default smoke queue processes 256 prompts for Llama/Gemma,
which exercises one complete Gemma batch of 224 plus a 32-prompt tail. Qwen
processes 64 prompts, producing eight complete batches of 8. Both Step 16 and
Step 17 receive the same limit. In `full` mode, neither step receives a prompt
limit. The script preflights every enabled model before starting the first run,
invokes `run_step16_17.sh` sequentially, and writes a master queue log and
status file under:

```text
02_OutputFiles/multi_model_logs/<queue_id>/
```

Run it inside an existing tmux session:

```bash
chmod +x /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_multi_model_inference.sh
bash /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_multi_model_inference.sh
```

The orchestrator does not create tmux sessions and never executes enabled
models concurrently on the same GPU.

To reuse existing Step 16 prompts, set this in the configuration section:

```bash
SKIP_STEP16=1

LLAMA31_PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/<llama_experiment>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<prompt_run_id>"
GEMMA12_PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/<gemma12_experiment>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<prompt_run_id>"
GEMMA26_PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/<gemma26_experiment>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<prompt_run_id>"
QWEN32_PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/<qwen_experiment>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<prompt_run_id>"
```

Only enabled models require a prompt path. The preflight verifies each
directory and its `prompt_units_manifest_v2.json` before starting the first
model. In `smoke` mode, only the model-specific Step 17 smoke limit is applied
to the existing prompt population. In `full` mode, Step 17 consumes the whole
existing manifest. Step 16 is neither executed nor compressed in this mode.

It is designed for the new RISE container/host workflow and does not use
Google Cloud, GCS, SSH, Docker, or bucket transfers.

Default persistent layout for the new RISE container:

```text
/tf/thesis_Santos/
  01_InputFiles/<experiment_id>/05_groups/<grouping_label>/
  02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<run_id>/
  02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/07_llm_outputs/<grouping_label>/<model>/<run_id>/
  02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/logs/<run_id>/
  03_Models/
  04_Steps/
    Step16/build_prompts.py
    Step17/run_llm_batch.py
    Step17/run_llm_batch_vllm.py
    Step17/summarize_llm_runtime.py
    Step17/test_run_llm_batch.py
    common/
    setups/
```

The script can be configured through environment variables such as:

```text
CLOUD_ROOT
VLLM_VENV
EXPERIMENT_ID
GROUPING_LABEL
RUN_ID
CONFIG_PATH
GROUP_DIR
PROMPT_DIR
PROMPT_MANIFEST
MODEL_DIR
MODEL_PATH
HF_MODEL_ID
BATCH_SIZE
DISABLE_THINKING
LIMIT_PROMPTS_S16
LIMIT_PROMPTS_S17
SKIP_STEP16
SKIP_STEP17
COMPRESS_STEP16
COMPRESS_STEP17
STEP16_ARCHIVE
STEP17_ARCHIVE
```

Step 17 output budgets come exclusively from each prompt unit's
`token_plan.planned_output_tokens`.

`DISABLE_THINKING=1` forwards `--disable-thinking` to the vLLM Step 17 runner.
Use it for models such as Qwen3 when the experiment requires non-thinking mode
and compact JSON outputs.

Wide Step 17 batch calibration on one fixed 1,500-prompt sample:

```bash
chmod +x /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/calibrate_step17_batch_sizes.sh

PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/exp_cicids2017_thursday_baseline_003/06_prompts/fixed_packet_count_size_006/<prompt_run_id>" \
CALIBRATION_LABEL="baseline003_fixed006_hybrid_wide_1500" \
BATCH_SIZES="16 32 64 96 128 160 188 224 256 320" \
LIMIT_PROMPTS_S17=1500 \
SAMPLE_METHOD="editable_count_stratified" \
/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/calibrate_step17_batch_sizes.sh
```

The calibration first builds one deterministic 1,500-prompt sample from the
complete manifest. For Baseline-003 the default sampler is
`editable_count_stratified`, so header-only, payload-only and mixed prompt
classes are represented. It then runs Step 17 sequentially, disables archive
creation, samples `nvidia-smi` once per second, and rewrites a comparison CSV
and Markdown file after every completed candidate under:

```text
02_OutputFiles/batch_calibration/<calibration_label>/
```

For vLLM runs, the launcher automatically activates:

```text
${CLOUD_ROOT}/.venv-vllm
```

Set `VLLM_VENV` only when the virtual environment is stored elsewhere.
Step 16-only runs with `SKIP_STEP17=1` do not require this environment.

Recommended first RISE smoke:

```bash
chmod +x \
  /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_step16_17.sh \
  /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/compression/compression_step_16.sh \
  /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/compression/compression_step_17.sh

CLOUD_ROOT="/tf/thesis_Santos" \
EXPERIMENT_ID="exp_cicids2017_thursday_baseline_003" \
GROUPING_LABEL="fixed_packet_count_size_006" \
RUN_ID="run_$(date -u +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)_rise_h100_baseline003_fixed006_hybrid_500prompts_batch168" \
CONFIG_PATH="/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/setups/config_LLM_baseline_003.json" \
BATCH_SIZE="168" \
LIMIT_PROMPTS_S17="500" \
/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_step16_17.sh
```

For the first Baseline-003 hybrid validation, run a smaller Step 17-only smoke
first if the full prompt population has already been uploaded/generated:

```bash
CLOUD_ROOT="/tf/thesis_Santos" \
EXPERIMENT_ID="exp_cicids2017_thursday_baseline_003" \
GROUPING_LABEL="fixed_packet_count_size_006" \
RUN_ID="run_$(date -u +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)_rise_h100_baseline003_fixed006_hybrid_smoke_100" \
CONFIG_PATH="/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/setups/config_LLM_baseline_003.json" \
PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/exp_cicids2017_thursday_baseline_003/06_prompts/fixed_packet_count_size_006/<prompt_run_id>" \
SKIP_STEP16=1 \
BATCH_SIZE="168" \
LIMIT_PROMPTS_S17="100" \
/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_step16_17.sh
```

By default, outputs produced by the current invocation are compressed after
Steps 16 and 17 finish successfully. Each archive contains only the current
run subtree, not previous runs stored under `06_prompts` or `07_llm_outputs`:

```text
02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/step16_prompts_<run_id>.tar.gz
02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/step17_llm_outputs_<run_id>.tar.gz
```

Only a step that actually ran is compressed. Set `COMPRESS_STEP16=0` or
`COMPRESS_STEP17=0` to disable either archive. `STEP16_ARCHIVE` and
`STEP17_ARCHIVE` override the archive paths.

To generate Step 16 prompts without starting inference, set:

```bash
RUN_MODE="smoke"  # limited prompt population
# RUN_MODE="full" # complete prompt population
SKIP_STEP16=0
SKIP_STEP17=1
```

The wrapper generates prompts sequentially for all enabled experiments and
compresses their Step 16 outputs when `COMPRESS_STEP16=1`. It does not invoke
the Step 17 backend or use the GPU for model inference. This mode can run in a
separate tmux session while another experiment is executing Step 17, provided
the processes use different experiment/output directories. Running both steps
with `SKIP_STEP16=1` and `SKIP_STEP17=1` is rejected as an invalid no-op.

The exported archives intentionally omit the final internal `run_id` directory
because the archive name or extraction directory already identifies the run.
After extraction, the relevant contents are therefore rooted at:

```text
06_prompts/<grouping_label>/
07_llm_outputs/<grouping_label>/<model_name>/
```

At exit, both successful and failed runs record their finish time and complete
launcher duration. The terminal log ends with `Run duration`, while
`status.txt` includes `finished_at`, `duration_seconds`, and `duration_human`.

Runtime note:

```text
The H100 path uses Step17/run_llm_batch_vllm.py. This is the active vLLM
adapter. It keeps the Step 17 validation/output logic from run_llm_batch.py
but loads Hugging Face model directories or ids with vLLM.
```

For a Step 16-only validation:

```bash
SKIP_STEP17=1 LIMIT_PROMPTS_S16=100 /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_step16_17.sh
```

For a Step 17-only run over an existing prompt directory:

```bash
SKIP_STEP16=1 \
PROMPT_DIR="/tf/thesis_Santos/02_OutputFiles/<experiment_id>/06_prompts/<grouping_label>/<run_id>" \
/tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/run_step16_17.sh
```

For comparisons between differently fragmented Flow-context-aware prompt
populations, use `build_paired_prompt_manifest_samples.py`. Unlike the
single-manifest sampler, it selects only common fragment-boundary blocks and
verifies that every output manifest covers exactly the same physical packet
IDs. The sample is deterministic and stratified by parent-flow packet count:

```bash
python3 /tf/thesis_Santos/04_Steps/build_paired_prompt_manifest_samples.py \
  --variant ctx4096=/path/to/ctx4096/prompt_units_manifest_v2.json \
  --variant ctx6144=/path/to/ctx6144/prompt_units_manifest_v2.json \
  --output-dir /path/to/paired_same_traffic_10000 \
  --target-packet-count 10000 \
  --seed flow_context_target_comparison_v1
```

The selected physical-packet count can differ slightly from the requested
target because the selector never cuts a Prompt Unit. Check
`paired_prompt_manifest_sample_report.json` before inference. The two output
manifests may contain different Prompt Unit counts; their physical packet sets
must be identical.
